# Falling platform (plain skin), native 32x10 frames fan1..fan4 (the frame names are the layout's; #236 redrew the old
# striped slab over a fan as forest wood). A lashed oak plank: its top row is the walk-and-grab straw `e1cfa5` (the
# "stand here" cue, ART_DIRECTION colour by meaning), the board brown, darker toward its underside, with a grain line and
# a knot. Two rope lashings wrap its front at x 3-4 and x 27-28, and the loose rope between them sags under the plank and
# sways a pixel right and left through the four frames (centre, right, centre, left): the plank hangs by a slack lashing.
# D71 at-rest cue, in every frame (#362): the split, an ink notch through the board at x 21-23, 2 px wide at the top and
# slanting to 1 px, with a pale splinter on each lip and a gap in the top (2 px) and the bottom (1 px) edge where it breaks
# through. The board ends show light end grain, not ink; the rope (L 0.57-0.71) and the straw are lighter than the moon
# rim's threshold, so the rim (D92) repaints only the underside's two ink ends (the split's own lips are `c`).
size 32 10
color k 211f30
# c: the split, the same ink as k; its own char so the moon rim (D92) never repaints it (forest_trap_sprites.RIM_KEEP).
color c 211f30
color S e1cfa5
color a 9a6a3c
color b 7a4e2a
color d 5a3720
color g 3e2616
color p c49060
color r b49e70
color R 8a7550
frame fan1
